d by the support team.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-18\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3117 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: System Info on the Overview Page\nDescription: The Overview page of a workspace has been enhanced with additional information that can be added to support tickets.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-18\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3118 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: CSRF Protection for Dynamic Destinations\nDescription: Today our approuters do not provide CSRF protection for dynamic destinations. It’s assumed that backends behind the destinations, handle CSRF protection on their own.   New security measures have been introduced to enable CSRF protection by the approuter. This is done by setting the CEP.EnableCsrfProtection property to true for all dynamic destinations where their respective backend doesn\",178\n\n\nOutput:\n", "role": "user"}], "parameters": {"model": "gpt-4o", "frequency_penalty": 0.0, "max_tokens": null, "n": 1, "presence_penalty": 0.0, "temperature": 0.0, "top_p": 1.0, "response_format": {"type": "json_object"}}}, "key": "chat_create_community_report_26bec8d6467cf9d4c19e837af9b464f1f516011088d500e1bfd50c42b8a8e85a_v2"}